WEBVTT


00:00:25.892 --> 00:00:28.417
Goodbyes can be bittersweet.


00:00:28.495 --> 00:00:31.430
It seems like only 306 days ago,


00:00:31.498 --> 00:00:34.262
we were snatched from our beloved
Central Park Zoo


00:00:34.334 --> 00:00:38.293
and dumped here in... rustic Madagascar.


00:00:38.371 --> 00:00:41.772
But now that we're leaving,
seeing you all here,


00:00:41.841 --> 00:00:45.299
it reminds us just
how many friends we've made.


00:00:49.182 --> 00:00:53.676
That's the greatest speech I've ever...!.


00:00:55.989 --> 00:00:58.389
Looks like the kid
can't hold his sea water.


00:00:58.491 --> 00:01:01.051
- Well, at least he showed up.
- I don't get it.


00:01:01.094 --> 00:01:03.062
It's not like Julien to miss a party.


00:01:03.129 --> 00:01:06.360
Maybe for some people,
saying goodbye is really hard.


00:01:07.300 --> 00:01:10.565
Yeah, well, send him a postcard
'cause the wind's right on schedule.


00:01:10.637 --> 00:01:12.434
Let's do this!.


00:01:12.505 --> 00:01:17.033
Can I have your attention? The redeye
to New York is about to board.


00:01:17.110 --> 00:01:19.271
We're going home for Christmas!.


00:01:19.846 --> 00:01:20.972
- Sandbags!.
- Check!


00:01:21.047 --> 00:01:22.344
- Ropes!
- Check!


00:01:22.415 --> 00:01:23.575
- Snacks!
- Check!


00:01:23.650 --> 00:01:25.447
- It's working!
- We did it!


00:01:25.518 --> 00:01:29.181
It may not be pretty,
but we headed to the city!


00:01:30.457 --> 00:01:35.019
Candied yams from Sylvia's!
That's what I want for Christmas.


00:01:35.095 --> 00:01:39.327
I can't wait to get back to my hippo
pool and that sweet smell of chlorine.


00:01:39.399 --> 00:01:44.336
And I can't wait to see Dr. Maneesh,
greatest chiropractor ever.


00:01:44.404 --> 00:01:48.101
Me? I just wanna see the snow
falling down on my beautiful city.


00:01:48.174 --> 00:01:51.439
New York, here we come!
What the...?


00:01:54.714 --> 00:01:56.045
Look out!


00:02:06.526 --> 00:02:09.359
Oh, no, no! No!
This isn't happening!


00:02:11.598 --> 00:02:12.997
Get off me! Get off me!


00:02:13.066 --> 00:02:14.693
Guys, did you hear something?


00:02:16.703 --> 00:02:19.604
- Cannibals!
- Cannibals! Where?!


00:02:19.672 --> 00:02:23.904
- Julien!
- It's just the freaks.


00:02:23.977 --> 00:02:26.912
Maurice, I thought they left already.


00:02:26.980 --> 00:02:29.210
I hope we're still charging them rent.


00:02:29.282 --> 00:02:33.082
- Mort, stop drumming already!
- Sorry.


00:02:33.153 --> 00:02:37.487
False alarm, everyone! Back into hiding.
It was just a cruel hoax.


00:02:37.557 --> 00:02:40.788
Hoax?! What kind
of sick joke is this, huh?!


00:02:40.860 --> 00:02:45.194
Sorry. We thought you were
the Marauding Red Night Goblin.


00:02:45.265 --> 00:02:47.199
The Marauding Red... What-nin?


00:02:47.267 --> 00:02:48.757
Maurice...


00:02:48.835 --> 00:02:52.532
Every year, on the 24th of Julianuary...


00:02:52.605 --> 00:02:55.130
- Julianuary?
- It's a festive holiday


00:02:55.208 --> 00:02:58.700
- named after His Majesty.
- It starts with a red glow.


00:02:58.811 --> 00:03:04.044
Then the air fills with the goblin's
horrible, mocking laughter.


00:03:04.083 --> 00:03:08.417
Then it pelts us
with hundreds of black rocks!


00:03:08.488 --> 00:03:10.820
Red Night Goblin!
The Red Night Goblin's coming!


00:03:10.890 --> 00:03:14.724
OK, I get it.
It's Picking on the King Day.


00:03:14.794 --> 00:03:15.920
Very funny.


00:03:18.164 --> 00:03:21.861
You can stop now, Mort.
I know it's you back there.


00:03:21.935 --> 00:03:24.165
The Red Goblin!


00:03:24.237 --> 00:03:25.864
- He's real!
- What's happening?!


00:03:27.774 --> 00:03:30.504
- Here, Julien.
- Hide the women and precious metal!


00:03:30.577 --> 00:03:34.638
Load the shooting thingy!
Fire at the Goblin!


00:03:35.848 --> 00:03:38.373
Lemurs down!
You, you, take their places.


00:03:38.451 --> 00:03:40.009
Aye, aye.


00:03:40.086 --> 00:03:42.213
That's it! I surrender!


00:03:42.288 --> 00:03:43.778
We're gonna die!


00:03:45.391 --> 00:03:49.088
- Alex, do something!
- All right, all right! All right.


00:04:02.842 --> 00:04:06.471
You're going down,
Red Night Marauding Goblin Guy!


00:04:10.216 --> 00:04:12.912
I did it, everybody!


00:04:12.986 --> 00:04:14.476
I did it!


00:04:20.960 --> 00:04:24.521
Everyone, after the Goblin.
Don't let him get away!


00:04:33.606 --> 00:04:36.336
- Candy canes?
- Presents?


00:04:38.011 --> 00:04:41.538
- These rocks taste like coal.
- Hang on a minute.


00:04:41.614 --> 00:04:45.015
Alex, I think you just shot down...


00:04:45.084 --> 00:04:48.747
Who's laughing now, Red Night Goblin?


00:04:51.190 --> 00:04:52.350
I am. That's who.


00:04:55.428 --> 00:04:57.328
Merry Madagascar!


00:04:59.499 --> 00:05:03.458
- I shot down Santa.
- You on the naughty list for sure, now.


00:05:04.771 --> 00:05:06.534
- Is it safe?
- Is what safe?


00:05:06.606 --> 00:05:09.803
Are there more of you? How many?
Tell me. Are you a robot?


00:05:09.876 --> 00:05:13.403
Maybe you have an army hidden inside
of you. Talk to me, robot army.


00:05:13.479 --> 00:05:17.381
- I am talking to you!
- That tickles.


00:05:18.151 --> 00:05:22.713
Look, everybody!
It shakes like a bowl full of jelly!


00:05:22.789 --> 00:05:26.350
- Hey, this is fun!
- Stop it, Julien! That's Santa Claus!


00:05:26.426 --> 00:05:29.589
- No wonder he throws coal at you.
- Santa who?


00:05:29.662 --> 00:05:32.654
Santa! Santa, you OK? I can't
believe I'm talking to Santa Claus!


00:05:32.732 --> 00:05:35.292
- I know.
- Wait. Who's Santa?


00:05:36.369 --> 00:05:39.395
What do you mean, "Who's Santa?"
If you're not Santa, who are you?


00:05:39.472 --> 00:05:42.339
My name is...


00:05:42.408 --> 00:05:43.875
I can't remember.


00:05:45.078 --> 00:05:47.410
Look, he's got another hat on.


00:05:47.480 --> 00:05:51.814
He must have hit his head in the crash.
Maybe he's got amnesia.


00:05:51.884 --> 00:05:54.785
Oh, this is bad. This is...
This is bad!


00:05:54.854 --> 00:05:58.381
I've ruined Christmas for everybody.
I've ruined Christmas for, like,


00:05:58.491 --> 00:06:01.085
the whole world! Unless...


00:06:01.127 --> 00:06:03.118
- Unless?
- Team huddle.


00:06:03.196 --> 00:06:05.130
This could work out great for everybody.


00:06:05.198 --> 00:06:07.598
- Santa's head wound?
- No, not his head wound.


00:06:07.667 --> 00:06:11.159
Here's the plan: we find the sleigh,
help Santa deliver the toys.


00:06:11.237 --> 00:06:14.172
Then, on the way home,
he drops us off in New York!


00:06:14.240 --> 00:06:16.367
It's perfect!
What do you guys think?


00:06:16.442 --> 00:06:17.739
- I'm in!
- OK.


00:06:17.810 --> 00:06:19.778
Let's go find that sleigh.


00:06:22.715 --> 00:06:27.049
They are just adorable! Alex,
go talk to them. Go, go, go, go, go!


00:06:27.120 --> 00:06:29.884
Hello, there, little reindeer.


00:06:29.956 --> 00:06:32.925
You guys up for a little road trip?
What do you say?


00:06:33.626 --> 00:06:37.528
Back away!
You don't know who you're dealing with.


00:06:37.597 --> 00:06:40.464
Hey, no need to get psycho.
They're just Santa's little...


00:06:40.533 --> 00:06:45.698
- We meet again, South Polers.
- North Polers.


00:06:47.473 --> 00:06:49.100
OK, you guys know each other?


00:06:49.175 --> 00:06:52.076
It's a cold war
that dates back centuries.


00:06:52.145 --> 00:06:55.979
You see, Santa used to be based
in the South Pole.


00:06:56.048 --> 00:07:00.246
This again? Santa chose North Pole,
fair and square.


00:07:00.353 --> 00:07:04.119
Please. They bribed him with candy canes
and cheap elf labor.


00:07:04.157 --> 00:07:05.886
That's it! Let's go!


00:07:05.958 --> 00:07:08.791
On my command, kick him in the bells.


00:07:08.861 --> 00:07:10.658
Wait, where's Private?


00:07:10.730 --> 00:07:13.722
You're the most beautiful deer
I've ever seen.


00:07:13.800 --> 00:07:17.964
That's the sweetest thing any penguin
has ever said to me.


00:07:28.214 --> 00:07:31.775
Shake it off, Private! That North Poler
might look like a tall drink of water,


00:07:31.851 --> 00:07:34.684
but she'll spit you out
like a cup of bad eggnog!


00:07:34.754 --> 00:07:38.656
Guys, guys. Come on, it's Christmas.
You know, the season of giving.


00:07:38.724 --> 00:07:41.420
So, what do you say?
Can you give us a ride?


00:07:41.494 --> 00:07:45.954
Son of the gun, we're only allowed
to take orders from Santa.


00:07:46.032 --> 00:07:50.298
Why don't you ask
your South Pole comrades to help?


00:07:50.369 --> 00:07:53.361
I forget! They can't fly.


00:07:54.340 --> 00:07:57.776
Merry Christmas down there,
stuck on the land!


00:07:57.877 --> 00:08:00.869
- Merry Christmas.
- Cupid!


00:08:03.015 --> 00:08:05.813
Great. There goes our lift home.


00:08:05.885 --> 00:08:07.876
- We'll fly it.
- Skipper, you're a penguin.


00:08:07.954 --> 00:08:10.718
And those reindeer have, like,
magical powers.


00:08:10.790 --> 00:08:13.486
That's exactly what
they want you to believe.


00:08:13.559 --> 00:08:15.891
Private, give 'em a little demo.


00:08:17.964 --> 00:08:20.831
The only thing magical
about those North Polers


00:08:20.900 --> 00:08:23.130
is that tank full of sparkly stuff.


00:08:23.202 --> 00:08:26.831
Now, go find Big Red,
and we'll get this baby airborne.


00:08:28.474 --> 00:08:34.071
Fat man, behold the beauty
of a traditional Julianuary carol


00:08:34.146 --> 00:08:36.614
honoring... me.


00:08:38.217 --> 00:08:42.483
- I like to
- Very nice.


00:08:42.555 --> 00:08:45.752
- You like to
- All together.


00:08:45.825 --> 00:08:49.283
We like to


00:08:49.362 --> 00:08:50.954
Move it


00:08:53.733 --> 00:08:56.224
I like to move it, move it


00:08:57.470 --> 00:08:59.199
Santa?


00:08:59.272 --> 00:09:03.106
I'm physically fit, physically fit
Physically, physically, physically fit


00:09:03.175 --> 00:09:04.267
Incoming!


00:09:05.645 --> 00:09:08.170
Alrighty, Santa. Time to big, big buddy.


00:09:08.247 --> 00:09:10.511
I don't wanna go!


00:09:10.583 --> 00:09:13.711
I just wanna shake my booty!


00:09:14.487 --> 00:09:17.388
- Santa, buddy. You gotta stop dancing.
- Santa!


00:09:19.125 --> 00:09:21.093
I'll never go!


00:09:22.061 --> 00:09:24.894
- What are we gonna do now?
- It's not gonna be Christmas Eve


00:09:24.964 --> 00:09:27.364
for much longer.
So either we go without Santa,


00:09:27.433 --> 00:09:30.129
- or the world goes without Christmas.
- That's right!


00:09:30.202 --> 00:09:33.262
You made this mess.
Now, we gotta clean it up.


00:09:33.339 --> 00:09:37.070
- Yo, Skipper! Sparkle time!
- All right, boys.


00:09:37.143 --> 00:09:40.510
Tighten your harnesses
and think happy thoughts.


00:09:42.848 --> 00:09:44.907
Viva Las Vegas!


00:09:57.897 --> 00:10:03.597
And everyone wept tears of joy
for the miracle that was Baby Julien.


00:10:03.669 --> 00:10:08.538
You see, fat man, Julianuary
is about the joy of giving.


00:10:08.608 --> 00:10:11.702
To me! Now, bring me the presents!


00:10:14.580 --> 00:10:16.673
Merry Julianuary.


00:10:16.749 --> 00:10:19.946
You remembered! Next one, please.
Move it along.


00:10:20.019 --> 00:10:22.852
Thank you, on behalf of His Majesty
and merry Julianuary.


00:10:23.756 --> 00:10:26.691
Thank you, on behalf of His Majesty
and merry Julianuary.


00:10:31.731 --> 00:10:34.757
- How did you do that?
- Beats me.


00:10:34.834 --> 00:10:38.099
- Could you make one for me?
- Merry Julianuary.


00:10:38.170 --> 00:10:39.694
- I want one.
- Me too.


00:10:40.706 --> 00:10:42.571
Next.


00:10:42.642 --> 00:10:44.337
Where's my presents?


00:10:44.410 --> 00:10:46.071
What's going on over there?


00:10:46.145 --> 00:10:48.272
Merry Julianuary!


00:10:48.347 --> 00:10:52.147
- Merry Julianuary.
- Merry Julianuary!


00:10:52.218 --> 00:10:55.654
- Merry Julianuary.
- Oh, no, no, no!


00:10:55.721 --> 00:10:56.710
Stop!


00:10:58.591 --> 00:11:04.359
What's so special about Julianuary
if everyone gets to have something?


00:11:04.430 --> 00:11:05.795
You!


00:11:05.865 --> 00:11:08.459
I took you in as my guest,


00:11:08.534 --> 00:11:12.334
and now, you've ruined Julianuary!


00:11:12.405 --> 00:11:14.066
From this moment forth,


00:11:14.140 --> 00:11:17.735
all your presents are my presents!


00:11:20.212 --> 00:11:24.979
Lady and gentlemen, we are about
to arrive at our first destination.


00:11:25.051 --> 00:11:27.815
Canada is straight ahead.


00:11:27.887 --> 00:11:30.151
OK, boys, let's take her down.


00:11:31.357 --> 00:11:32.585
Flaps up.


00:11:32.658 --> 00:11:35.718
Beaks down. Stay on target.


00:11:35.795 --> 00:11:37.888
Stay on target!


00:11:45.504 --> 00:11:46.903
What kind of landing was that?


00:11:46.972 --> 00:11:50.135
Any landing you can walk away from
is a good landing.


00:11:50.676 --> 00:11:53.577
This is stupid, Marty.
Can't we just use the front door?


00:11:53.646 --> 00:11:57.207
Come on. How hard can it be?
Melman, you're up!


00:11:57.283 --> 00:11:59.012
- But I'm claustrophobic.
- Yeah?


00:11:59.118 --> 00:12:01.780
Now, you can be Santa Claustrophobic.


00:12:01.821 --> 00:12:05.120
Now, dive, fool, dive, dive, dive!


00:12:05.191 --> 00:12:07.421
Easy...


00:12:07.493 --> 00:12:08.926
Guys? I'm stuck!


00:12:09.862 --> 00:12:12.854
Hang in there, Melman!
I'm coming!


00:12:12.932 --> 00:12:14.923
- Melman, I'm right here!
- I'm burning!


00:12:15.000 --> 00:12:18.333
- You're not burning!
- Help!


00:12:19.205 --> 00:12:20.570
Thank you.


00:12:22.208 --> 00:12:23.539
Don't leave me!


00:12:23.609 --> 00:12:26.271
Alex, you still have the present!


00:12:30.282 --> 00:12:32.876
Dash away, boys. Dash away!


00:12:32.952 --> 00:12:35.580
- What...? No, wait!
- Hang on!


00:12:37.022 --> 00:12:38.922
I got you, Melman!


00:12:42.061 --> 00:12:44.552
Way to drop the ball, you hippie freak.


00:12:44.630 --> 00:12:46.621
Me? Melman lost it in the chimney.


00:12:46.699 --> 00:12:50.396
Calm down. It's a small town,
there's only a couple more houses.


00:12:50.469 --> 00:12:52.664
- Let's not freak out.
- Oh, yeah?


00:12:54.406 --> 00:12:56.670
Can we freak out now?!


00:12:56.742 --> 00:12:57.834
OK, here's the plan.


00:12:57.943 --> 00:13:00.912
We head to the nearest post office
and we just dump the gifts.


00:13:00.946 --> 00:13:02.937
- That's a plan.
- I need stamps, anyway.


00:13:03.015 --> 00:13:05.609
Skipper, get us
to the nearest post office.


00:13:05.684 --> 00:13:06.776
In New York.


00:13:16.195 --> 00:13:18.390
Well, looks like our coffee break.


00:13:20.432 --> 00:13:25.233
Oh, my gosh. Oh, my gosh! Oh, my gosh!
Oh, my gosh! You're Santa's helpers!


00:13:25.304 --> 00:13:28.364
This is amazing!
You're hairier than I thought.


00:13:28.440 --> 00:13:32.308
But amazing! OK, calm down, Abby.
Breathe.


00:13:32.378 --> 00:13:35.347
Namaste. Namaste.


00:13:36.081 --> 00:13:39.380
Merry Christmas! Merry Christmas!
Merry Christmas!


00:13:39.451 --> 00:13:40.713
Merry Christmas!


00:13:42.154 --> 00:13:44.145
Oh, my gosh! I almost forgot!


00:13:48.127 --> 00:13:49.424
I made you cookies.


00:13:54.466 --> 00:13:56.366
This is the best Christmas ever.


00:13:57.937 --> 00:14:00.030
Don't tell Santa I was up. Really.


00:14:00.105 --> 00:14:01.629
OK, I'm going to bed now.


00:14:01.707 --> 00:14:05.575
I can't go to sleep. No way I can go
to sleep. I just met Santa's helpers!


00:14:06.779 --> 00:14:08.679
I think I broke my collarbone.


00:14:08.747 --> 00:14:11.181
No! It's OK. Going to bed now.


00:14:11.250 --> 00:14:13.013
Oh, my gosh! Oh, my gosh! Oh, my gosh!


00:14:16.322 --> 00:14:19.018
New plan. We're not
going to the post office anymore.


00:14:19.091 --> 00:14:21.116
We're Santa's hairy helpers.


00:14:21.193 --> 00:14:25.254
And we don't rest until every one
of these gifts gets delivered.


00:14:47.353 --> 00:14:50.254
Skipper, progress report.


00:14:50.322 --> 00:14:54.349
Only 1 52 cities left to go.


00:14:55.961 --> 00:14:57.428
Skipper, look!


00:15:00.299 --> 00:15:02.597
- New York!
- It's still here!


00:15:02.668 --> 00:15:05.466
- It's still beautiful!
- And it's still gonna be here


00:15:05.537 --> 00:15:07.027
when we're done!


00:15:07.106 --> 00:15:10.007
All right, New York, let's do this!


00:15:15.080 --> 00:15:19.312
On the 88th day of Julianuary


00:15:19.385 --> 00:15:22.047
My true love sent to me


00:15:22.121 --> 00:15:26.956
A great, big present for me


00:15:27.026 --> 00:15:31.986
Oh, Amelia. Did you ever feel
like you're just wasting away?


00:15:34.500 --> 00:15:37.958
This is the worst Julianuary ever.


00:15:39.705 --> 00:15:41.536
- King Julien?
- Hello.


00:15:41.607 --> 00:15:44.838
Haven't you heard of knocking?
I could have been naked in here.


00:15:44.910 --> 00:15:48.277
I'm sorry if I ruined your Julianuary.


00:15:48.347 --> 00:15:50.713
I don't understand.


00:15:50.783 --> 00:15:55.413
I have all the presents.
Why do I feel so empty inside?


00:15:55.487 --> 00:15:57.853
I don't know. But back there,


00:15:57.957 --> 00:16:00.653
when we were all
giving presents to each other,


00:16:00.693 --> 00:16:02.923
it was pretty good.


00:16:02.995 --> 00:16:07.659
Hey! Why don't you give one
to your girlfriend Amelia over there.


00:16:07.733 --> 00:16:10.998
- I bet she'd like it.
- No, she's not my girlfriend.


00:16:11.070 --> 00:16:15.871
I don't want to. OK, fine, I'll do it!
Keep your chubby hands off.


00:16:15.941 --> 00:16:19.433
Here, Amelia. Merry Julianuary.


00:16:20.279 --> 00:16:22.144
Look at the smile on Amelia.


00:16:24.283 --> 00:16:27.411
Making her feel good
makes me feel good.


00:16:27.486 --> 00:16:30.785
Kind of warm and tingly
on the inside.


00:16:30.856 --> 00:16:33.347
Like pinworms! Come, fat man!


00:16:33.425 --> 00:16:36.588
We must share with the world
what I have discovered!


00:16:40.299 --> 00:16:41.664
We did it.


00:16:41.734 --> 00:16:46.068
Every single present delivered
and accounted for.


00:16:46.138 --> 00:16:49.369
Goodbye, empty bags.
Hello, new...


00:16:49.441 --> 00:16:52.899
No! There's still a few left
in this one!


00:16:52.978 --> 00:16:55.811
No. No! No more!
I can't take it.


00:16:55.881 --> 00:16:58.611
I'll throw it in the river.
It'll be like we never saw them.


00:16:58.717 --> 00:17:00.082
Give me that.


00:17:00.119 --> 00:17:02.053
Wait, they're... they're for us.


00:17:02.121 --> 00:17:03.110
- What?
- Melman.


00:17:03.188 --> 00:17:04.177
- Really?
- Marty.


00:17:04.256 --> 00:17:06.349
- Get out of here.
- Alex! And me!


00:17:06.425 --> 00:17:09.656
No way! Candied yams from Sylvia's!


00:17:09.728 --> 00:17:12.356
And they're still hot!
They're still hot.


00:17:12.431 --> 00:17:16.231
An inflatable hippo pool?
And chlorine?!


00:17:16.735 --> 00:17:18.600
Oh, yeah. That's the stuff.


00:17:18.670 --> 00:17:21.264
Dr. Maneesh's neck massager!


00:17:21.340 --> 00:17:24.867
- What'd you get, Alex?
- Snow falling down


00:17:24.943 --> 00:17:28.208
on my beautiful city.
How did he know?


00:17:28.280 --> 00:17:32.114
That's why Santa's Santa.
The big man's got some talent.


00:17:32.184 --> 00:17:35.449
We can't leave him back there dancing
around with that bump on his head.


00:17:35.521 --> 00:17:38.490
- We gotta go back and help him.
- The good news is there's enough


00:17:38.557 --> 00:17:42.084
sparkly stuff to get us
back to Madagascar.


00:17:42.161 --> 00:17:45.961
- Is there bad news?
- Only enough to get to Madagascar.


00:17:46.031 --> 00:17:47.020
Put it back!


00:17:47.099 --> 00:17:52.059
So it's Madagascar or... home?


00:17:57.943 --> 00:18:00.104
There she is, fellas!


00:18:01.647 --> 00:18:06.016
Maybe next Christmas, New York.
Skipper, full speed ahead!


00:18:06.552 --> 00:18:09.385
This is the life.


00:18:12.524 --> 00:18:16.722
It says, "To Mort. Happy Julianuary.


00:18:16.795 --> 00:18:18.319
Love, King Julien."


00:18:18.397 --> 00:18:21.457
A coconut! Thank you, King Julien!


00:18:21.533 --> 00:18:24.229
OK, boys, let's take her down.


00:18:24.303 --> 00:18:26.362
We just lost one of our engines!


00:18:26.438 --> 00:18:29.771
I thought you said there was enough
sparkly stuff to get us there!


00:18:29.842 --> 00:18:31.434
- I did.
- Then what happened?


00:18:31.510 --> 00:18:32.841
I was wrong!


00:18:34.246 --> 00:18:37.306
Red Night Goblin!
The Red Night Goblin's coming!


00:18:41.186 --> 00:18:44.622
Come on, Private. Think happy thoughts.
Happy thoughts.


00:18:52.331 --> 00:18:54.856
The Red Night Goblin's attacking again!


00:18:54.933 --> 00:18:56.491
Brace for impact!


00:19:00.405 --> 00:19:02.430
Oh, no.


00:19:07.112 --> 00:19:08.704
He's alive!


00:19:11.583 --> 00:19:14.609
Where am l? The children.
The presents!


00:19:14.686 --> 00:19:18.452
- He got his memory back.
- Terrible crisis, Santa!


00:19:18.524 --> 00:19:21.288
The South Polers stole sleigh
for joyride!


00:19:21.360 --> 00:19:23.920
- Now, Christmas is ruined!
- What?!


00:19:23.996 --> 00:19:27.295
That's an outright Christmas lie
with all the trimmings.


00:19:27.366 --> 00:19:30.335
Yeah, Christmas isn't ruined.
We delivered everything.


00:19:30.402 --> 00:19:34.133
It's the truth. Santa,
the South Polers saved Christmas.


00:19:34.206 --> 00:19:35.400
Cupid, stay out of this!


00:19:36.909 --> 00:19:39.810
I grow tired of your reindeer games.


00:19:39.878 --> 00:19:42.676
We want to be... bipolar.


00:19:43.182 --> 00:19:45.082
Son of the gun.


00:19:45.150 --> 00:19:49.484
- So you really delivered all the gifts?
- It's the least we could do.


00:19:49.555 --> 00:19:52.046
And you even found Liechtenstein?


00:19:52.424 --> 00:19:53.413
Liechety-what?


00:19:54.660 --> 00:19:58.619
Oh, chestnuts! Those children
will be up any minute now!


00:19:58.697 --> 00:20:01.757
- This way, Santa.
- But there's no sparkly stuff left.


00:20:01.833 --> 00:20:04.427
I'll use the reserve tank then.


00:20:04.503 --> 00:20:07.438
- Oh, reserve tank.
- Hey, Santa, wait!


00:20:07.506 --> 00:20:10.304
- My friends and l...
- Thank you all for everything!


00:20:10.375 --> 00:20:12.104
- Santa, wait!
- If that sleigh leaves


00:20:12.177 --> 00:20:14.202
and you're not with Santa,
you'll regret it.


00:20:14.279 --> 00:20:17.874
- Farewell, Private.
- We'll always have Madagascar!


00:20:17.950 --> 00:20:19.349
- Santa!
- Wait!


00:20:19.418 --> 00:20:24.720
And Julien, you're officially
off the naughty list!


00:20:24.790 --> 00:20:28.521
What? You can't take me
off the naughty list.


00:20:28.594 --> 00:20:31.324
I am the naughty list!


00:20:31.396 --> 00:20:32.590
What's the naughty list?


00:20:32.664 --> 00:20:35.155
Merry Christmas!


00:20:36.802 --> 00:20:39.396
Well, looks like Santa's
back in business.


00:20:39.471 --> 00:20:42.133
And we're back in Madagascar.


00:20:42.207 --> 00:20:45.301
And you know what? We're gonna
have the best Christmas ever.


00:20:45.377 --> 00:20:46.401
Right here!


00:20:53.685 --> 00:20:57.678
This'll get me back on the naughty list.
Coconut ball fight!


00:21:02.294 --> 00:21:04.262
All right, let's give
these babies a spin.


00:21:04.329 --> 00:21:07.321
I can't stop! I can't stop!


00:21:08.700 --> 00:21:11.828
Rockefeller Center
ain't got nothin' on this!


00:21:12.537 --> 00:21:15.233
Well, we may not have
gotten home for Christmas,


00:21:15.307 --> 00:21:17.537
but we got snow!


00:21:17.609 --> 00:21:19.600
I wouldn't do that if I were you.


00:21:20.545 --> 00:21:24.208
- It's not snow! It's not snow!
- See, Marty? It's not what you get.


00:21:24.283 --> 00:21:27.047
- It's what you give.
- Give it a rest!


00:21:27.986 --> 00:21:31.615
I'm so naughty.
Mort, you're next!


00:21:32.257 --> 00:21:34.452
Alex, you OK?


00:21:35.627 --> 00:21:37.117
Who's Alex?


00:21:38.130 --> 00:21:42.396
Merry Christmas and happy Julianuary,
everybody!

